From 5ecb57e38cbe9452eca34e6cdb6ef60ea224ac63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:18:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms, nvidia-drm: NV_HDMI_3D_AVI_CTA_VIC: the CTA VIC in the
 AVI InfoFrame next to a half 3D layout

NVKMS names 3840x2160 at 24, 25 and 30 Hz and 4096x2160 at 24 Hz by
their HDMI_VIC for a display whose HF-VSDB does not say UHD_VIC: the EDID
parser puts the HDMI_VIC timings first (prioritizeEdidHDMIExtTiming()),
ValidateModeIndexEdid() looks among the CTA-861 timings first only for
frame packing or UHD_VIC, and such a mode goes out with VIC 0 in the AVI
InfoFrame (NvTiming_ConstructVideoInfoframeCtrl()) and the HDMI_VIC in
NVKMS's own vendor InfoFrame (ConstructVSInfoFrameCtrl()). nvidia-drm
lists no side-by-side or top-and-bottom modes, so a client tells the
display of such a layout with an HDMI 1.4b vendor InfoFrame through
NV_HDMI_VSIF_METADATA, which goes out in the place of NVKMS's own
(SendVendorSpecificInfoFrame()). That one carries the 3D structure and,
by HDMI 1.4b, no HDMI_VIC (the two exclude each other: "only one of those
can be supplied", hdmi_vendor_infoframe_check_only() of Linux). In those
modes the display was told a 3D structure of no format, so a client could
not tell it of 3D there.

Linux names the format of such a 3D mode by its CTA VIC in the AVI
InfoFrame: drm_mode_hdmi_vic() gives no HDMI_VIC to a mode with a 3D
layout ("No HDMI VIC when signalling 3D video format"), so
drm_mode_cea_vic() gives the CTA VIC, and i915 and amdgpu send the AVI
and vendor InfoFrames that drm makes of the mode. NVKMS now does the
same: the AVI InfoFrame carries the CTA VIC of the format (93, 94 and 95
for 3840x2160 at 24, 25 and 30 Hz, 98 for 4096x2160 at 24 Hz, as for
HDR10+ and Dolby Vision in these modes), next to the client's vendor
InfoFrame, on every HAL, only:
 - with a client's HDMI 1.4b vendor InfoFrame of side by side (half,
   3D_Ext_Data 0, as Linux sends it) or top and bottom
   (nvHadesHalfLayoutVsif());
 - to a display whose EDID declares that 3D structure for that CTA VIC as
   do_hdmi_vsdb_modes() of Linux reads it: 3D_Structure_ALL with 3D_MASK
   over the first sixteen SVDs, or a 2D_VIC_order entry with its
   3D_Structure (side by side with 3D_Detail 1), of every HDMI VSDB
   (nvHadesEdidRead3D(), nvHadesEdidDeclares3D()).
That is the rule of Linux, for a display of HDMI 1.4 as for one of HDMI
2.0: a format declared in 3D is an SVD of a video data block, and
vic_for_avi_infoframe() keeps a VIC that the sink lists there whatever the
sink. Everything else is as before: other 3D structures, frame packing
(NVKMS's own HDMI 3D), 2D, Dolby Vision and HDR10+.

The kernel log says, once in each mode set and again where it changes,
how a client's 3D vendor InfoFrame is signalled in such a mode and why:
"3D side by side (half) in a mode that NVKMS names by HDMI_VIC 3: the AVI
InfoFrame says CTA VIC 93 and the client's vendor InfoFrame the 3D
structure, as Linux signals a 3D mode (its EDID declares side by side
(half) for VIC 93, an SVD of its video data block)", or why the AVI
InfoFrame keeps VIC 0 (another 3D structure, or not declared).

nvidia-drm gives each connector that takes NV_HDMI_VSIF_METADATA the
read-only property NV_HDMI_3D_AVI_CTA_VIC (1), so that a client knows
that it can tell such a display of a half layout in those modes.
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c |  12 +
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c       |  16 +
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-priv.h      |   2 +
 src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-hades.h      | 303 ++++++++++++++++++
 src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h      |  17 +-
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-hdmi.c           | 149 +++++++--
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-modeset.c        |   9 +
 7 files changed, 479 insertions(+), 29 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c
index 29c1750..d6b86b0 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c
@@ -1722,6 +1722,12 @@ nv_drm_connector_new(struct drm_device *dev,
                                            nv_dev->nv_connector_hdmi_dv_hdmi14b_property,
                                            0);
             }
+            /* Hades: the CTA VIC in the AVI InfoFrame next to a half 3D layout */
+            if (nv_dev->nv_connector_hdmi_3d_avi_cta_vic_property) {
+                drm_object_attach_property(&nv_connector->base.base,
+                                           nv_dev->nv_connector_hdmi_3d_avi_cta_vic_property,
+                                           1);
+            }
         }
 
         if (nv_dev->nv_connector_allm_capable_property) {
@@ -2097,6 +2103,12 @@ void nv_drm_connector_add_dual_mode_tmds(struct nv_drm_connector *nv_connector)
                                        nv_dev->nv_connector_hdmi_dv_hdmi14b_property,
                                        0);
         }
+        /* Hades: the CTA VIC in the AVI InfoFrame next to a half 3D layout */
+        if (nv_dev->nv_connector_hdmi_3d_avi_cta_vic_property) {
+            drm_object_attach_property(&nv_connector->base.base,
+                                       nv_dev->nv_connector_hdmi_3d_avi_cta_vic_property,
+                                       1);
+        }
     }
 #endif
 
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c
